<Project Sdk="Assimalign.Cohesion.Sdk.IdentityHub">
	<!--
		A plain IdentityHub program: no platform or application-model package.

		BookStore's identity AppHost names a database for this hub, identity-db, so the hub has no store tier: the
		database's program is the project beside this one, BookStore.Identity.Database ([proposed] in v2, §8.9; §15,
		decision 46). Whether publishing this project still builds the store tier's image is an open question of v2
		(§15): as v2 §8.9 is written it does, and nothing deploys that image.

		For a hub with no database declared, Sdk.IdentityHub also builds the private database's store tier at publish,
		as a second image (bookstore-identity-identityhub-store), with no code from this project in it, and the program
		in that image runs a small host of IdentityHub's own. The owner decided both on 2026-11-23 (v2 §15, row 9). The
		designer counts one more thing as chosen with the second answer, because the owner was shown it first: that the
		program is one generated call into IdentityHub's own store entry (v2 §1). [proposed] in v2 (§8.9): the names of
		that entry and of that host, the image's name, and its fingerprint (the Cohesion version, the entry, the RID and
		the format labels), by which it changes only when Cohesion does.
	-->
</Project>
